  "application_type_full": "Householder planning permission",
  "description": "The property at 5 Doctors Close is a mid-terrace house, with front of the house facing West, and the rear of the house facing East. Attached to the North and South walls of the house are neighbouring houses in the terrace.\nOn the east-facing (\"Rear\") of the house is a conservatory and beyond it a rear garden stretching to the edge of the property.\n\n\nThe proposed build is to create a permanent extension from the eastern facing (\"Rear\") wall of the house, the current conservatory will be dismantled.\n\nThe proposed extension build will be box shaped, of the following dimensions:\n3m total length extended eastward from the eastern \"rear\" wall of the house\n3m total height from ground level\n5m total width, so that it is in line with the outer walls of the house\n\nConstruction details and dimensions:\nThe North wall of the extension will be 3m length X 3m height, 20cm width constructed from red brick and concrete pour\nThe South wall of the extension will be 3m length X 3m height, 20cm width constructed from red brick and concrete pour\nThe roof of the extension will be a flat solid roof 3m length X 5m height, constructed of wood, insulation panels, felt and roof tiles. The roof will have a skylight in the center made of double-glazed glass pane\nThe floor of the extension will be a level surface 3m length X 5m width, made of concrete pour and covered with wooden tiles\n\nThe eastward-facing \"rear\" of the extension will be constructed of:\nA double door in the middle made of double-glazed glass\nTwo \"dwarf walls\" 1m height X 1.5m width on either side of the door, connecting to the North and South walls\nAbove the dwarf walls, connecting to the roof will be four windows made of double-glazed glass\n",
